# headlessui-tabs

## Description
Rules and best practices for implementing accessible, fully customizable tab interfaces using Headless UI's `TabGroup`, `TabList`, `Tab`, `TabPanels`, and `TabPanel`.

## Version
1.0.0

---

## Rule "Install Headless UI"

### Description
Ensure the package is installed before using components.

### Trigger
```txt
npm install @headlessui/react
```

---

## Rule "Basic Structure"

### Description
Use the correct nesting structure: TabGroup > TabList > Tab, and TabPanels > TabPanel.

### Snippet
```tsx
import { Tab, TabGroup, TabList, TabPanel, TabPanels } from '@headlessui/react'

<TabGroup>
  <TabList>
    <Tab>Tab 1</Tab>
    <Tab>Tab 2</Tab>
    <Tab>Tab 3</Tab>
  </TabList>
  <TabPanels>
    <TabPanel>Content 1</TabPanel>
    <TabPanel>Content 2</TabPanel>
    <TabPanel>Content 3</TabPanel>
  </TabPanels>
</TabGroup>
```

---

## Rule "Styling with data-* attributes"

### Description
Use data-selected and data-hover to apply styles conditionally.

### Snippet
```tsx
<Tab className="data-hover:underline data-selected:bg-blue-500 data-selected:text-white">
  Tab 1
</Tab>
```

---

## Rule "Styling with render props"

### Description
Use render props for fine-grained state-based styles.

### Snippet
```tsx
<Tab as={Fragment}>
  {({ selected, hover }) => (
    <button className={clsx(selected && 'bg-blue-500 text-white', hover && 'underline')}>
      Tab 1
    </button>
  )}
</Tab>
```

---

## Rule "Disable a Tab"

### Description
Use the `disabled` prop to prevent interaction.

### Snippet
```tsx
<Tab disabled className="disabled:opacity-50">
  Tab 2
</Tab>
```

---

## Rule "Vertical Tabs"

### Description
Add the `vertical` prop to TabGroup and style TabList as a column.

### Snippet
```tsx
<TabGroup vertical>
  <TabList className="flex flex-col">
    <Tab>Tab 1</Tab>
    <Tab>Tab 2</Tab>
  </TabList>
  <TabPanels>
    <TabPanel>Content 1</TabPanel>
    <TabPanel>Content 2</TabPanel>
  </TabPanels>
</TabGroup>
```

---

## Rule "Manual tab activation"

### Description
Use `manual` on TabGroup to prevent automatic selection via arrow keys.

### Snippet
```tsx
<TabGroup manual>
  <TabList>
    <Tab>Tab 1</Tab>
    <Tab>Tab 2</Tab>
  </TabList>
  <TabPanels>
    <TabPanel>Content</TabPanel>
  </TabPanels>
</TabGroup>
```

---

## Rule "Default selected tab"

### Description
Use `defaultIndex` to preselect a tab.

### Snippet
```tsx
<TabGroup defaultIndex={1}>
  <TabList>
    <Tab>Tab 1</Tab>
    <Tab>Tab 2</Tab>
    <Tab>Tab 3</Tab>
  </TabList>
  <TabPanels>
    <TabPanel>Content 1</TabPanel>
    <TabPanel>Content 2</TabPanel>
    <TabPanel>Content 3</TabPanel>
  </TabPanels>
</TabGroup>
```

---

## Rule "Controlled tabs"

### Description
Use `selectedIndex` and `onChange` for controlled tab behavior.

### Snippet
```tsx
const [index, setIndex] = useState(0)

<TabGroup selectedIndex={index} onChange={setIndex}>
  <TabList>
    <Tab>Tab 1</Tab>
    <Tab>Tab 2</Tab>
  </TabList>
  <TabPanels>
    <TabPanel>Content 1</TabPanel>
    <TabPanel>Content 2</TabPanel>
  </TabPanels>
</TabGroup>
```

---

## Rule "Render custom components"

### Description
Use `as` prop to render elements with custom or non-default HTML tags.

### Snippet
```tsx
<TabList as="aside">
  <Tab as="button">Tab 1</Tab>
  <Tab as="button">Tab 2</Tab>
</TabList>
```

---

## Rule "Keyboard support"

### Description
Understand default keybindings: arrows, home/end, enter/space with `manual`.

### Details
- **Arrow keys**: switch tabs (left/right or up/down with vertical)
- **Home/End**: jump to first/last
- **Enter/Space (manual only)**: activates selected tab